+- **FQ115. How many weeks ahead the days are made.** Spec 05 says "Generate upcoming occurrences several weeks ahead" and gives no number. Every day already made is announced and never moves (FQ61), so a membership change starts only in the first week after the last made day: the number is also the shortest wait for a change, and a new member's first day comes after it. It is the longest the worker can be stopped before a member has no next date, too.
+    - Default: four weeks. The worker keeps each confirmed day's dates made through the date 28 days after the club's today (`packages/domain/src/schedule/generate.ts`, `HORIZON_DAYS`). It is the number the contract's fixtures already took (`packages/contracts/src/fixtures/world.ts`, `changeFrom`: seen from Friday 6 November 2026, every day to Saturday 5 December is announced, and the mock's membership change starts on Monday 7 December), so the server and the mock the app is built against agree.
+    - The other readings: three weeks, the smallest "several", which shortens a change's wait by a week and needs the fixtures' change moved to Monday 30 November in a contract PR; or a looser reading of "announced" (FQ61), which would let a change start before days nobody has added to.
+    - The cost of four: someone added to a club waits four to five weeks for the change to start. A day is never made late: a worker stopped for more than four weeks skips the days whose 7 AM passed meanwhile, and they show as no date, never as a day born open (spec 04).
+    - Needed by: B2 (`api/b2-generation`; the membership change, `api/b2-membership-change`).
 
